
This is a really stupid way to play roulette. To be honest, there is
no smart way to play. The only way to win is to not play.

The code schadenfreude.c should similate this moronic algorithm.

Put a $5 chip on every black square. Then put a $5 chip on every split
that is beside the black square and provides a red number.

The layout of the American stupid roulette table looks like this : 

    -------------------------------------------------------------+
   / |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |
  /  | 3r | 6b | 9r | 12r| 15b| 18r| 21r| 24b| 27r| 30r| 33b| 36r|
 /   |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |
+ 00 +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+
|    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |
+----+ 2b | 5r | 8b | 11b| 14r| 17b| 20b| 23r| 26b| 29b| 32r| 35b|
|    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |
+  0 +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+
 \   |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |
  \  | 1r | 4b | 7r | 10b| 13b| 16r| 19r| 22b| 25r| 28b| 31b| 34r|
   \ |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |
    -------------------------------------------------------------+


So if we place an bet ( X ) on every black square : 


    -------------------------------------------------------------+
   / |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |
  /  | 3r | 6b | 9r | 12r| 15b| 18r| 21r| 24b| 27r| 30r| 33b| 36r|
 /   |    |  X |    |    |  X |    |    |  X |    |    |  X |    |
+ 00 +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+
|    |  X |    |  X |  X |    |  X |  X |    |  X |  X |    |  X |
+----+ 2b | 5r | 8b | 11b| 14r| 17b| 20b| 23r| 26b| 29b| 32r| 35b|
|    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |
+  0 +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+
 \   |    |  X |    |  X |  X |    |    |  X |    |  X |  X |    |
  \  | 1r | 4b | 7r | 10b| 13b| 16r| 19r| 22b| 25r| 28b| 31b| 34r|
   \ |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |
    -------------------------------------------------------------+


Also a bet on every split on a black number that adds in a red number
in a unique way  : 


    -------------------------------------------------------------+
   / |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |
  /  | 3r X 6b | 9r | 12r| 15bX 18r| 21rX 24b| 27r| 30r| 33bX 36r|
 /   |    |  X |    |    |  X |    |    |  X |    |    |  X |    |
+ 00 +----+----+--X-+--X-+----+----+----+----+--X-+--X-+----+----+
|    |  X |    |  X |  X |    |  X |  X |    |  X |  X |    |  X |
+----+ 2b | 5r | 8b | 11b| 14r| 17b| 20b| 23r| 26b| 29b| 32r| 35b|
|    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |
+  0 +--X-+--X-+----+----+--X-+--X-+--X-+--X-+----+----+--X-+--X-+
 \   |    |  X |    |  X |  X |    |    |  X |    |  X |  X |    |
  \  | 1r | 4b | 7r X 10b| 13b| 16r| 19r| 22b| 25rX 28b| 31b| 34r|
   \ |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |
    -------------------------------------------------------------+

In this way we have every black number covered as well as all of the red
numbers. That is all the squares on the board with the obvious exception
being those nasty green zeros.

Lets look at the probability of a "win" here.  We have 38 numbers on the
wheel when we include the 36 regular numbers and the 0 and double 00. I
can tell you that the little bouncing ball is blind and does not see if
there is a red landing spot or a green or black. That silly thing has no
real clue at all. So firstly lets consider the classic red black issue
where some dumb mook only ever bets on red and black and also the idiot
plays with a Martingale betting strategy. That always wins right? If you
have enough of a bankroll and the table has no limits then sure. Good
luck with that.

There are 18 red numbers and 18 black numbers with a wheel of 38 total
possible results and thus the probability p() of a red number : 

             p(Rw) = 18 / 38 = 0.47368421

Here we see the probability of a red number is a bit better than 47%
and surely anyone can see the same result for black.  In general the
casino ( the house ) always wins with a slight edge that gives 52.6%
to the casino. However wait. What if we cover all of the black numbers
as above and toss in the splits that provide a red number?

That is the full list of all black numbers with the red split neighbours
with no consideration to the results from a roulette wheel.  We have two
situations or questions : what is the probability of a "win" and to what
degree is the "win" actually worth winning?  Is it possible, in fact is
it probable that a "win" is a financial loss?  Yes. The numbers are very
clear here and easy to simulate with a bit of software.  However firstly
we need the basic win/loss probabilities.  The most easy thing on the 
table ( no pun intended ) is where are the losers?  Clearly the zero
squares are both losers and that means 0 and 00 green numbers are going
to wipe out the whole table.

We know that every single bet we made on a black square will result in a
direct 35:1 type pay off as well as an additional 17:1 for a split. Are
there any numbers that are different? Of course. All of the red numbers
are less of a payoff by a large margin.

But wait.

That 35 factor pay off with the added 17 is only for a black number. We
can say that black numbers matter here. Almost every red number is very
similar to a Black Jack surrender in that you get the 17:1 pay off and
lose everything else.  For the sake of being detailed lets look at the
actual loss and win numbers for this crazy sort of roulette bet :


     number            pay out                    With $5 chips
    ------------------------------------------------------------
     green  0          total loss                             0
     green 00          total loss                             0
     red    1          17                                    85
     black  2          35 + 17                              260
     red    3          17                                    85
     black  4          35 + 17                              260
     red    5          17                                    85
     black  6          35 + 17                              260
     red    7          17                                    85
     black  8          35 + 17                              260
     red    9          17                                    85
     black 10          35 + 17                              260
     black 11          35 + 17                              260
     red   12          17                                    85
     black 13          35 + 17                              260
     red   14          17                                    85
     black 15          35 + 17                              260
     red   16          17                                    85
     black 17          35 + 17                              260
     red   18          17                                    85
     red   19          17                                    85
     black 20          35 + 17                              260
     red   21          17                                    85
     black 22          35 + 17                              260
     red   23          17                                    85
     black 24          35 + 17                              260
     red   25          17                                    85
     black 26          35 + 17                              260
     red   27          17                                    85
     black 28          35 + 17                              260
     black 29          35 + 17                              260
     red   30          17                                    85
     black 31          35 + 17                              260
     red   32          17                                    85
     black 33          35 + 17                              260
     red   34          17                                    85
     black 35          35 + 17                              260
     red   36          17                                    85

How many of the above are maximum value 260? Well those are the black
numbers. So we already know the percentage there is 47.368 or at best
a little worse than fifty percent. Everything else is very likely a
loss.  There are a total of 36 bets on the table and the very best
one may hope for is a 47% win. Every other possibility is a loss and we
see the 0 and double 00 as a disaster.

However lets look at the probabilities : 

          disaster =  2/38 = 0.05263157 =  5.26%
         red split = 18/38 = 0.47368421 = 47.37%
           perfect = 18/38 = 0.47368421 = 47.37%

The sum of those probabilities has to be 1 exactly unless we consider
the bizarre situation where the roulette balls jumps out of the track
and onto the floor somewhere. However that results in nothing happening
except for a scramble around to find the little white ball and then toss
it in the trash. Sort of like dice at a craps table one should, in theory,
throw away a little red die that made a leap for the floor. That never
happens.  Regardless the total bet on the table has to be $170 in order
to cover all those numbers and the splits.  There is a 47.37% chance that
you lose a large piece of that with only $85 payout.

So a dumb question that is perfectly unreasonable is what happens
if a schmuck walks into a casino with a bankroll of $2000 and then
plays this situation? The math will always tell us that the house
wins and over any period of time you go broke. However, what if there
is a rull to walk away when $500 has been won or lost. Should be easy
to simulate with some decent RNG source.

For the sake of another discussion we will use the Mersenne Twister
as the PRNG here.  Mostly because it is entirely repeatable. As you
may know we can also use drand48() with a set seed value and get a
very repeatable sequence of random numbers also.  Unless we use a
radiation decay source then a pseudo random number sequence is all
we can expect. Another possible approach is to determine the current
time on a computer and use that data as a seed to something reasonable
such as drand48().

